    airo:evidenceText "A robot crushed a worker at a Volkswagen production plant in Germany, the company said Wednesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "241" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2d5c46867766> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Prosecutors have already opened an investigation into the matter." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "258" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/36cc71d0566c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While the internet hysteria over this worker's death is heavily comprised of dark comedy, many, such as Musk and Bill Gates, share concerns that the technology of robots is outstripping our regulation of them." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "251" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3cc70ec0067e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Currently, there isn't a lot of information available on the details of the case, but it is being investigated by German authorities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "261" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51871422152d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As a matter of procedure necessary to have the body released in cases of non-natural death, the state prosecutor's office said it is investigating to rule out any criminal culpability." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "254" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d0396b56a5a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the Financial Times, prosecutors are already investigating the incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "259" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a7856a65299e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But the state prosecutor’s office in Kassel said that had not yet been confirmed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d2781672942f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A 22 year old man was yesterday killed by a robot at a Volkswagen plant in Baunatal, Germany." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "245" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/df16def4e420> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Kassel regional prosecutor's office said it's investigating whether negligence may have been involved and, if so, who was culpable." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "257" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7360c7dc597> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Prosecutors are investigating the worker's death, but the internet has already begun to call it the first robot homicide." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "251" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e79eeda6449a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The robot had been the property of the Meissen-based firm for whom the man worked and the machine had not yet been handed over to Volkswagen, the car company told reporters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "248" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9d4ba3f24aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Then we'll see if — and if so, against whom — charges are to be made,\" a spokesman for the prosecutor's office told the German news agency Deutsche Presse-Agentur." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "257" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/efceece698af> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The second known case was in Japan in 1981, when Kenji Urada, an engineer at a Kawasaki factory, was pushed into a grinding machine by a broken robot he was working on." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "250" .

