    airo:evidenceText "A technician has been killed by a robot in an accident at a Volkswagen plant near Kassel, Germany, reports the Financial Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "259" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8583558238d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 years later, a man was killed as he tried to fix a robot at a Kawasaki Heavy Industries plant in Japan." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "263" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/486a6b56afe5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The first is thought to have occurred in 1979, when a worker died after being struck in the head by the arm of a one-ton production-line robot at a Ford plant in Flat Rock, Michigan, US." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "263" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/010832157f7e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The incident occurred on Monday as a Volkswagen factory in Baunatal, Hesse, when the 21-year-old man from another company was working on assembling the robot for a new electric motor production line." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "248" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e48ad6bf731> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr Blay Whitby, lecturer in artificial intelligence at the University of Sussex, said: 'It's important to understand that with present technology we cannot 'blame' the robot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "263" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/64f148b9f834> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Future of Life Institute (FLI) , funded in part by a $10 million donation from Tesla CEO Elon Musk, announced its plans to use $7 million to fund various projects aimed at controlling artificial intelligence." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "251" .

